From ca26a1f5ec22dcf4c8a78088b76796e13ba50975 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Larsson <banan@ludd.ltu.se>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:22:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: raise the xPON service table to 256 entries

The xPON service array is a software classification list walked at transmit
time to pick the GEM port, T-CONT and queue. It is not a hardware table, and
its entries are not scarce hardware resources: every rule an OLT installs can
share one GEM port and one T-CONT, differing only in UNI and priority.

Thirty-two entries are therefore consumed by a handful of UNIs at eight
priorities each, after which the agent rolls the whole service set back and
the datapath stays down. Raise the array to sixty-four.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Project <openwrt-devel@lists.openwrt.org>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
index ab63920af2ef..6d301a4a81b6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -34,7 +34,13 @@
 #define AIROHA_FE_MC_MAX_VLAN_TABLE	64
 #define AIROHA_FE_MC_MAX_VLAN_PORT	16
 #define AIROHA_NUM_TX_IRQ		2
-#define AIROHA_XPON_MAX_SERVICES	32
+/*
+ * Software classification rules rather than a hardware table: one entry per
+ * UNI and priority combination, all of which can share a single GEM port and
+ * T-CONT. An OLT mapping eight priorities across several UNIs, plus a virtual
+ * Ethernet interface point, needs far more than the thirty-two this started with.
+ */
+#define AIROHA_XPON_MAX_SERVICES	256
 #define HW_DSCP_NUM			2048
 #define IRQ_QUEUE_LEN(_n)		((_n) ? 1024 : 2048)
 #define TX_DSCP_NUM(_n) 	\
-- 
